#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133503 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ec34a19-988a-5421-8c05-6bb4c5a9e366" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Minimum Possible Value Using the Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality"}] :question/id #uuid "77b63ba5-410b-536c-8ed0-92c895097cc9" :question/math-academy-id "e-5554" :question/problem "Consider the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/assets/d1a095e61e6ea64f97a105fd69bc07f3f44990cd6d9794e54e355463c37a2413.png) Given that $\\mathbf{u}\\cdot \\mathbf{v}=-12$ and $\\Vert \\mathbf{v}\\Vert =4,$ what is the smallest possible value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality,\n\n$$\n\\vert \\mathbf{u}\\cdot \\mathbf{v} \\vert \\leq \\Vert \\mathbf{u} \\Vert \\cdot \\Vert \\mathbf{v} \\Vert.\n$$\n\nWe are given all the quantities in the inequality above, except for $\\Vert \\mathbf{u} \\Vert.$ So first, we compute $\\Vert \\mathbf{u} \\Vert$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(\\sqrt{k})^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6+k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u\\cdot v| & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ |-12| & \\le \\sqrt{6+k}\\cdot (4) \\\\ 12 & \\le 4\\sqrt{6+k} \\\\ 3 & \\le \\sqrt{6+k} \\\\ {3}^{2} & \\le (\\sqrt{6+k})^{2} \\\\ 9 & \\le 6+k \\\\ 3 & \\le k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $k$ is $3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133504 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6bde92b0-4e98-5c2e-848e-7a5febc848ae" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Acute Angle Between Two Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "763f7e8e-081a-57ad-825f-601a38fe3984" :question/math-academy-id "e-5555" :question/problem "Find the acute angle between the vectors ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/assets/5ed21f4bb536757026315cce838f4cc3028493adac2ff29d46a5b8cbdf11170b.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/assets/8d813e104a708be37ba44b9448806f49ea21a16fe7f613314d2eeab2b59bbda2.png)" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula\n\n$$\n\\cos\\theta = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{w}}{\\Vert\\mathbf{v}\\Vert \\, \\Vert \\mathbf{w}\\Vert},\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 2+(-4)\\cdot (-2)+(-2)\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-2)^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{25}\\cdot \\sqrt{16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{5\\cdot 4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta=\\arccos \\left( \\dfrac{1}{2} \\right)=\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133554 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b56b45b-94dd-5ba1-aae6-6b17cffaf532" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cosine of an Angle"}] :question/id #uuid "0562751a-55be-5fd1-83d2-11795ba7a052" :question/math-academy-id "e-5910" :question/problem "Let $A(-2, 4, -2, 2)$ and $B(4, 0, -1, -4).$ Find the cosine of the angle $\\angle{AOB},$ where $O(0,0,0,0)$ is the origin." :question/worked-solution "First, let\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=\\overset{\\to }{OA}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,b=\\overset{\\to }{OB}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, let $\\theta = m\\angle{AOB}$ be the angle between the vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}.$ Then, we can find $\\cos \\theta$ using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{‖a‖\\,‖b‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{1}{b}_{1}+{a}_{2}{b}_{2}+{a}_{3}{b}_{3}+{a}_{4}{b}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{1}^{2}+{a}_{2}^{2}+{a}_{3}^{2}+{a}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{b}_{1}^{2}+{b}_{2}^{2}+{b}_{3}^{2}+{b}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)\\cdot 4+4\\cdot 0+(-2)\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot (-4)}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-4)^{2}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{-14}{\\sqrt{28}\\cdot \\sqrt{33}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-14}{\\sqrt{14}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{33}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{33}} \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{33}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326794 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ec34a19-988a-5421-8c05-6bb4c5a9e366" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Minimum Possible Value Using the Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e7f2884-41de-57a7-8921-e979c1a4a379" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326796} {:answer/id #uuid "0c03f4dd-1ae3-5d87-a6c7-165eaad3c42c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326797} {:answer/id #uuid "4a0d810d-7493-56d0-84a4-a31d78f6fe29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326798} {:answer/id #uuid "4029df03-4e8d-5743-952e-048bd153230e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326799} {:answer/id #uuid "1f005a33-f229-524a-8a75-75ccbf62bd89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326800}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c03f4dd-1ae3-5d87-a6c7-165eaad3c42c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326797} :answer-field/id #uuid "47c0c6c1-d73c-572c-9079-7b9e87b07d76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326795}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d7867427-d2e2-5ec2-b2db-9610afb9d5c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-140440" :question/problem "Given that $‖u‖=5$ and $u\\cdot v=-15$, find the smallest possible value of $‖v‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u\\cdot v| & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ |-15| & \\le 5\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ 15 & \\le 5\\cdot ‖v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply both sides of the inequality by $\\frac{1}{5}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 15 & \\le \\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 5\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ 3 & \\le ‖v‖\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖v‖$\nis  $3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326801 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ec34a19-988a-5421-8c05-6bb4c5a9e366" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Minimum Possible Value Using the Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b37de58-cc57-5d52-9620-ab00fca7db29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326803} {:answer/id #uuid "eb52230c-c6b9-53b1-965b-2ec48ceb1af8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326804} {:answer/id #uuid "092c1770-40b4-5200-acd8-d8b6fcfb42dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326805} {:answer/id #uuid "ae4aaa0b-f1e5-5d31-b9d0-5485760c459e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326806} {:answer/id #uuid "b9ef760c-9ca5-5bb8-aa91-f0f99a504f2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae4aaa0b-f1e5-5d31-b9d0-5485760c459e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326806} :answer-field/id #uuid "28d7794b-d1ba-56c6-9faa-0739793d10a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326802}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0af8185f-9e08-5662-8cee-2aec5a72ed44" :question/math-academy-id "q-140442" :question/problem "Consider the vector $u=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ \\sqrt{k} \\\\ -\\sqrt{k} \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$ Given that $u\\cdot v=-2$ and $‖v‖=1$, what is the smallest possible value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality,\n\n$$\n|u\\cdot v|\\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖.\n$$\n\nWe are given all the quantities in the inequality above, except for $‖u‖.$ So first, we compute $‖u‖$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(\\sqrt{k})^{2}+(-\\sqrt{k})^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2+2k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u\\cdot v| & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ |-2| & \\le \\sqrt{2+2k}\\cdot (1) \\\\ 2 & \\le \\sqrt{2+2k} \\\\ {2}^{2} & \\le {(\\sqrt{2+2k})}^{2} \\\\ 4 & \\le 2+2k \\\\ 2 & \\le 2k \\\\ k & \\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $k$ is $1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326808 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b56b45b-94dd-5ba1-aae6-6b17cffaf532" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cosine of an Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8838e5fa-5f97-5a64-bc47-bfa4b7983c83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{22}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326810} {:answer/id #uuid "51996b6c-222d-5450-abdf-f041d8ccc81a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{132}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326811} {:answer/id #uuid "5fd2e6ca-32f8-53e1-b1b4-8628a23b2ef1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{132}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326812} {:answer/id #uuid "1f934f6f-6e95-57c5-a7d1-28ea6070e152" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{22}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326813} {:answer/id #uuid "31f41a8a-ba68-5d70-a6b1-f961dfbefa5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{22}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326814}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5fd2e6ca-32f8-53e1-b1b4-8628a23b2ef1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{132}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326812} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffdc6b88-736f-50db-9d3b-df2b11e520c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326809}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "41b261c3-9f5f-5508-8cac-5fa8af188eb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-140455" :question/problem "Let $A(1,0,-1,2)$ and $B(4,8,2,-2).$ Find the cosine of the angle $∠AOB$, where $O(0,0,0,0)$ is the origin." :question/worked-solution "First, let\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=\\overset{\\to }{OA}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,b=\\overset{\\to }{OB}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, let $\\theta =m∠AOB$ be the angle between the vectors $a$ and $b.$ Then, we can find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{‖a‖\\,‖b‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{1}{b}_{1}+{a}_{2}{b}_{2}+{a}_{3}{b}_{3}+{a}_{4}{b}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{1}^{2}+{a}_{2}^{2}+{a}_{3}^{2}+{a}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{b}_{1}^{2}+{b}_{2}^{2}+{b}_{3}^{2}+{b}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 4+0\\cdot 8+(-1)\\cdot 2+2\\cdot (-2)}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{8}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{88}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{22}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{132}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326815 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b56b45b-94dd-5ba1-aae6-6b17cffaf532" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cosine of an Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6f75180-9d09-5b40-8b2b-4fc32df56efd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{38}{7\\sqrt{30}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326817} {:answer/id #uuid "f0f3aa12-6aad-55da-a7fb-de00dae1736a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{7\\sqrt{30}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326818} {:answer/id #uuid "86c2855f-bcb8-51da-b62a-919cf201330d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{\\sqrt{30}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326819} {:answer/id #uuid "71cd5b1b-2599-5755-b620-3dc575e9b467" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{30}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326820} {:answer/id #uuid "5d5eee5a-707a-5466-92b1-0989f3be06ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{75}{14\\sqrt{30}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326821}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6f75180-9d09-5b40-8b2b-4fc32df56efd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{38}{7\\sqrt{30}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326817} :answer-field/id #uuid "78bb470b-f267-5720-a815-7921706cd0ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326816}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ab53b11a-f41d-5f0a-ae52-61c8789440eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-140456" :question/problem "Let $A(1,1,-1,-1)$, $B(2,4,6,8)$, and $C(1,2,3,4).$ Find the cosine of the angle $∠BAC.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $v=\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $w=\\overset{\\to }{AC}.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =b-a \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w & =c-a \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $\\theta =m∠BAC$ be the angle between the vectors $v$ and $w.$ Then, we can find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{‖v‖\\,‖w‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 0+3\\cdot 1+7\\cdot 4+9\\cdot 5}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{7}^{2}+{9}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{5}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{76}{\\sqrt{140}\\cdot \\sqrt{42}} \\\\  & =\\frac{76}{2\\sqrt{35}\\cdot \\sqrt{42}} \\\\  & =\\frac{76}{14\\sqrt{30}} \\\\  & =\\frac{38}{7\\sqrt{30}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326822 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ec34a19-988a-5421-8c05-6bb4c5a9e366" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Minimum Possible Value Using the Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80eb29b8-3991-5560-bb52-0566e8cbaea1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326824} {:answer/id #uuid "59099e77-63ec-54ff-8558-1f776bd10c5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326825} {:answer/id #uuid "39632596-f778-55ad-b2bc-1664410c519f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326826} {:answer/id #uuid "dcfb5fc3-8825-56c8-a76a-c19f11ea1076" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326827} {:answer/id #uuid "cc2bf5db-aee3-5546-836e-c65c1b9b5b96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326828}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39632596-f778-55ad-b2bc-1664410c519f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326826} :answer-field/id #uuid "e07b573e-cc7f-500d-b0ea-d4e770c3ac23" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326823}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1ef711bf-e75f-55d6-b13d-2b815f8dde92" :question/math-academy-id "q-39430" :question/problem "Given that $‖u‖=3$ and $u\\cdot v=4$, find the smallest possible value of $‖v‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u\\cdot v| & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ |4| & \\le 3\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ 4 & \\le 3\\cdot ‖v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply both sides of the inequality by $\\frac{1}{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 4 & \\le \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 3\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ \\frac{4}{3} & \\le ‖v‖\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖v‖$\nis  $\\frac{4}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134220 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6bde92b0-4e98-5c2e-848e-7a5febc848ae" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Acute Angle Between Two Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97cc1fdd-98a8-5bf1-9c19-10d1b030350f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131763} {:answer/id #uuid "d32c97cf-14bd-5909-ad5e-22b0d7893ce1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2π}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131764} {:answer/id #uuid "fe9b2474-1e81-5d5f-8ac8-d161e7f86ed7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131765} {:answer/id #uuid "37937909-c96a-5f1c-850c-7bd754012ec2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131766} {:answer/id #uuid "39656d9c-29c1-512b-804e-e26c58da22f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97cc1fdd-98a8-5bf1-9c19-10d1b030350f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131763} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e53e492-d10b-5e23-9082-e19792c12e4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131762}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "706daa06-6654-51cd-8ce5-90b88ebad445" :question/math-academy-id "q-40559" :question/problem "Find the acute angle between the vectors $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}].$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Using the formula\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{‖v‖\\,‖w‖},\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot (-1)+(-\\sqrt{5})\\cdot 1+7\\cdot 5+1\\cdot \\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-\\sqrt{5})^{2}+{7}^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}+(\\sqrt{5})^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{\\sqrt{64}\\cdot \\sqrt{32}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{32}}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326829 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6bde92b0-4e98-5c2e-848e-7a5febc848ae" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Acute Angle Between Two Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66108ab3-56bc-534a-906d-99d3d35fdea6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{15.25}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326831} {:answer/id #uuid "77e63f4a-640c-530c-9e16-421046d4426a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{60.01}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326832} {:answer/id #uuid "338b645f-6ccb-5813-85a7-7086a2a0715e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{68.12}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326833} {:answer/id #uuid "c7b4704f-1df6-5926-bd90-26411ca01c39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{33.87}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326834} {:answer/id #uuid "669132da-705b-54aa-8ce2-87c50f92e20c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{60.67}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "338b645f-6ccb-5813-85a7-7086a2a0715e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{68.12}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326833} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0478840-afd9-567a-a5e1-88ba5ae1f156" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326830}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e95b32a7-e640-5e72-ba43-44f6c02564cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-40561" :question/problem "Rounded to two decimal places, what is the acute angle between the vectors  $v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{‖v‖\\,‖w‖},\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)(-1)+(2)(-1)+(3)(2)+(-4)(0)}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{30}\\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{6})≈{68.12}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326836 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6bde92b0-4e98-5c2e-848e-7a5febc848ae" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Acute Angle Between Two Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2da36d87-7ea0-50f5-ad0b-8e86905a120e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{62.39}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326838} {:answer/id #uuid "af329fc1-3bad-562a-9686-364daea3486e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{65.41}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326839} {:answer/id #uuid "45fab55d-faba-592e-ac78-f13946e8899e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{75.28}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326840} {:answer/id #uuid "27388a2f-afc2-512f-b141-21d7548abc62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{76.11}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326841} {:answer/id #uuid "e056d305-1a96-51a1-b4f3-b5a3da6e0f44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{82.33}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27388a2f-afc2-512f-b141-21d7548abc62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{76.11}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326841} :answer-field/id #uuid "5db9d1d7-01c1-5dbb-a504-a8730e257cc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326837}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "963dc6f1-4812-5ffd-b9fd-b83e98ae8cbc" :question/math-academy-id "q-40564" :question/problem "Rounded to two decimal places, what is the acute angle between the vectors  $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ \\text{ }-2\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula  \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{‖v‖\\,‖w‖},\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-4)+(-2)\\cdot 1+(-4)\\cdot (-2)+(-2)\\cdot (-2)}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-2)^{2}}\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{25}\\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{6}{25})≈{76.11}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326843 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6bde92b0-4e98-5c2e-848e-7a5febc848ae" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Acute Angle Between Two Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bc29b77-914c-5a98-aa37-c5cc7af410ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi }{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326845} {:answer/id #uuid "53fc6357-c900-5f23-84a3-727d206fda35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326846} {:answer/id #uuid "800068e3-a506-52e0-9c5f-7a9689996022" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326847} {:answer/id #uuid "2b0a35ea-d51e-5d9b-8149-11810edb781a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326848} {:answer/id #uuid "27c9c57e-764c-537c-b3de-f8dc8050a9a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/re